    },
    "baseline": "Captured in installation claim transaction before async resolution: approved active hash + versionId + activationId. Actual Git tree must equal verified release tree. An unselected different tree rejects. Rechecked before source adoption, in queue transaction, before review and in activation transaction. Old approved release cannot authorize a fresh selection after rollback. The baseline also shares the existing drain write transaction, before fencing executions; loaded module identity is reused.",
    "persistence": "No new schema/table/queue. Internal exact-release mode uses existing installation receipt. Baseline retained in ModuleVersion.report until its normal version-history retention; propose/build/recovery/approval activation read it. Git objects and candidate/release refs remain.",
    "ordinaryUpdate": "Existing submitMergedCommit/mergeModuleUpstream unchanged."
  },
